Where this implementation comes from
------------------------------------

No third-party source code is included in this project. The implementation
was written against published specifications and vendor documentation, which
are listed here so that any part of it can be traced back to its source.

RNDIS protocol (rndis/)
    [MS-RNDIS]: Remote Network Driver Interface Specification (RNDIS)
    Protocol, published by Microsoft under its Open Specifications terms,
    which permit copying the document to build implementations of the
    technology it describes. Message layouts, OIDs, status codes and the
    control-channel class requests come from there.

    Remote NDIS To USB Mapping, Microsoft Windows driver documentation, for
    how the control channel rides on endpoint 0 and how data records are
    carried on the bulk endpoints.

DriverKit driver (driver/, app/)
    Apple's NetworkingDriverKit and USBDriverKit documentation, and the
    sample "Connecting a network driver", for the driver lifecycle, the
    packet pool and queue model, and the system-extension install flow.

USB matching
    USB-IF assigned class, subclass and protocol codes, and the descriptors
    a device reports about itself.
